From 470b41a0cb532ac3d422d99a9a5e961361863a22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mano Thanabalan <mano.thanabalan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 15:09:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] radio_planner: stop the TCXO only when no task is running
 after the arbiter
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Both post-dispatch arbiter calls (the general path's post-callback
arbiter and the no-task branch added in the earlier patch) can LAUNCH a
task — the launch callbacks re-start the TCXO and configure the chip.
The unconditional smtc_modem_hal_stop_radio_tcxo() at the tail of
rp_callback then immediately killed that clock: the chip stayed in RX
MODE WITH A DEAD OSCILLATOR — status reads reported RX while the chip
demodulated nothing (bench 2026-09-02: hwrx frozen 10-58s spans every
1-2 minutes, nodes voting alone in 1/3 tallies while peers heard their
votes; hearing resumed only after the next SPI activity nudged the
chip). Whether a re-arm launched via the enqueue-inline arbiter (TCXO
kept, worked) or via a dispatch arbiter (TCXO killed, deaf) depended on
flag timing — hence the alternating deaf/hearing windows.

Now the TCXO/ant-switch shutdown only runs when no task is RUNNING
after the arbiter; the stop still happens on the dispatch that later
ends that task.
---
 smtc_rac_lib/radio_planner/src/radio_planner.c | 18 +++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/smtc_rac_lib/radio_planner/src/radio_planner.c b/smtc_rac_lib/radio_planner/src/radio_planner.c
index af70c88..89c1973 100644
--- a/smtc_rac_lib/radio_planner/src/radio_planner.c
+++ b/smtc_rac_lib/radio_planner/src/radio_planner.c
@@ -603,9 +603,21 @@ void rp_callback( radio_planner_t* rp )
             rp_task_arbiter( rp, __func__ );
         }
 
-        smtc_modem_hal_set_ant_switch( false );
-        // Shut Down the TCXO
-        smtc_modem_hal_stop_radio_tcxo( );
+        // SuperLexicon patch 0007: shut the TCXO down ONLY when no task is
+        // running. Both arbiter calls above (the general path's post-callback
+        // arbiter and this no-task branch) can LAUNCH a task whose launch
+        // callbacks re-start the TCXO and put the chip in RX — the
+        // unconditional stop immediately after killed that clock, leaving
+        // the chip IN RX MODE WITH A DEAD OSCILLATOR: status reads RX,
+        // hwrx frozen, the node deaf for tens of seconds until the next
+        // SPI activity nudged it (bench 2026-09-02: hwrx=0 spans of 10-58s
+        // every ~1-2 min, one consensus window lost per incident).
+        if( rp->tasks[rp->radio_task_id].state != RP_TASK_STATE_RUNNING )
+        {
+            smtc_modem_hal_set_ant_switch( false );
+            // Shut Down the TCXO
+            smtc_modem_hal_stop_radio_tcxo( );
+        }
     }
 }
 
